.TH IMUD\-PROMETHEUS 8 "2026-08-05" "imud 1.8.2" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
imud\-prometheus \- Prometheus exporter for the imud IMU daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B imud\-prometheus
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B imud\-prometheus
connects to
.BR imud (8)'s
local binary stream socket and serves the latest fused state as Prometheus
text-format gauges on
.B GET /metrics
\(em attitude, heading (magnetic and, when declination is known, true), rate
of turn, heave and heave rate, the sea-state statistics (significant wave
height, wave/roll/pitch periods and amplitudes), the compass-health metrics
.RB ( imud_mag_anomaly_ratio ", " imud_mag_residual_radians ),
gyro bias, quiescence, temperature, and the packet flag bits as 0/1 gauges
.RB ( imud_mag_valid ", " imud_converged ", " imud_heave_valid ", "
.BR imud_wave_valid ", " imud_engine_on ).
.B imud_up
reports whether a live packet is held and
.B imud_packets_total
counts frames received.
.PP
All gauges are base SI units (radians, metres, seconds, \(deC); heading is
additionally exported in conventional degrees. Sea-state gauges read 0.0
until the statistics settle; periods also read 0.0 when becalmed or not
rolling \(em that is the measurement, not an error.
.PP
The exporter is pull-based: scrapes are answered from the cached newest
sample, and the request is read non-blocking from the same
.BR poll (2)
that watches the imud stream, so a slow scraper never wedges the stream
reader. A client that connects and sends nothing is dropped after 2 seconds.
One scrape is served at a time. It reconnects to
imud automatically and answers scrapes with
.B imud_up 0
while imud is away. Built on the ABI-stable
.BR libimud (3)
\(em no rebuild needed across imud wire revisions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Config file (default:
.IR /etc/imud/imud\-prometheus.conf ).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/imud/imud\-prometheus.conf
Configuration; see
.BR imud\-prometheus.conf (5).
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload the config (log level; the listen address needs a restart).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR imud (8),
.BR imud\-prometheus.conf (5),
.BR libimud (3)
.SH AUTHORS
Richard Simpson
